glycated hemoglobin(HbA1c) \< 9% and \>9 %, baseline and 4 (+-2)days after drug exposure.|rate of hypoglycemia during coronary care unit stay., Rate of capillary glucose \<70 mg/dL and \<40 mg/dL,evaluated by capillary glucose measurements by point-of-care tests,during CCU stay(expected average of 1 week)., baseline up to 1 week .|total of insulin doses requirement during coronary care unit stay., Comparison of the total requirement of correctional insulin between treatment and control arms after drug exposure., baseline up to 1 week .|incidence of composite end-point., Comparison the incidence of composite end-point between two arms.Composite end-point include:

